+## archive-logs.sh
 
-Archives are pruned by hand today.
+```
+bin/archive-logs.sh [--keep-days N] SERVICE [SERVICE...]
+```
+
+Packs the logs of each named service from `logs/SERVICE` into a dated tarball,
+`archives/SERVICE-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz` (UTC date). It runs from cron on the log host every
+night. Paths are resolved relative to the repository, not the current directory.
+
+- **Several services:** list them all in one invocation, e.g.
+  `bin/archive-logs.sh web api`. Service names must match `[a-z0-9][a-z0-9_-]*`; all
+  names are validated before anything is archived. A service without a log directory is
+  an error and the run exits non-zero.
+- **`--keep-days N`:** after all new archives are in place, delete archives in
+  `archives/` older than N days (by modification time). This covers every
+  `*-YYYYMMDD.tar.gz` file in the directory, not only the services named in this run.
+  Nothing is pruned if archiving fails. Without the option, nothing is deleted.
+- **Summary:** on success one line is printed, e.g.
+  `archived 2 service(s): web api; pruned 3 archive(s) older than 30 day(s)`
+  (the `pruned` part appears only with `--keep-days`). Errors go to stderr.
+
+Exit status: 0 on success, 1 if archiving fails, 64 for a usage error.
+
+Requires Bash 4.4+ and GNU `find`/`tar`. Running twice on the same day overwrites that
+day's archive.
